    "title": "Vanessa Trump issues fierce ultimatum to boyfriend Tiger Woods after shocking DUI arrest: report",
    "text": "Vanessa Trump allegedly gave her boyfriend, Tiger Woods, a telling ultimatum after he was arrested for driving under the influence. “She’s not happy at all. She’s both disappointed and a little bit pissed, if I’m being honest,” an insider close to the couple told the Daily Mail on Saturday. “It’s a definite red flag, and she told him that he’s going to get this sorted out and that she’s going to require that,” the source added. Vanessa Trump reportedly issued an ultimatum to her boyfriend, Tiger Woods (seen above with his girlfriend), after his DUI arrest. X/@TigerWoods “It’s a definite red flag, and she told him that he’s going to get this sorted out and that she’s going to require that,” an insider told the Daily Mail Saturday. (Pictured: Trump in January.) AFP via Getty Images “He has to get things under control, or she’s not going to stick around,” they added. The insider told the outlet that Trump, 48, is a “concerned girlfriend expressing boundaries and saying that he’s got to get his s–t together, like right now.” The pro golfer, 50, is reportedly “very apologetic” and “wants to fix” his errors. “He has to get things under control, or she’s not going to stick around,” the source added. (Seen here: Trump and Woods hugging.) X/@TigerWoods Woods (seen here in his mug shot) was arrested on Friday. Getty Images “He’s embarrassed. He’s mortified at all this,” the source continued. “And this is really humiliating for it to happen again. And Vanessa is embarrassed, too. All her friends are like, ‘Girl, what the hell?'” Trump, meanwhile, didn’t comment on Woods’ arrest when she returned to social media over the weekend to share a video of her eldest daughter, Kai. The couple, who were first romantically linked last March, were last seen packing on the PDA at a golf match last Tuesday. The pro golfer was involved in a rollover crash (seen above). AP The athlete (seen above in a car) was photographed leaving jail later that day. Christopher Oquendo for NY Post Want more celebrity and pop culture news? Start your day with Page Six Daily. Thanks for signing up! A rep for Woods wasn’t available to Page Six for comment. The athlete was arrested after he was involved in a rollover car accident while in Jupiter Island, Fla., at around 2 p.m. local time on Friday. According to cops, Woods’ breathalyzer test was negative. However, he allegedly showed “signs of impairment.” Woods (seen here in July 2025) took a breathalyzer test and the result was negative. Getty Images The billionaire and Trump (seen hugging above) have been dating since last year. GREG LOVETT/PALM BEACH POST / USA TODAY NETWORK via Imagn Images He was ultimately arrested after refusing “a urinalysis test, leading to charges of DUI with property damage and refusal to submit to a lawful test,” Martin County Sheriff John Budensiek said. Woods was seen with bloodshot eyes in his mug shot and was later photographed leaving the Martin County jail hours after his arrest. In the snaps, the PGA golfer appeared disappointed as he sat in the front seat of an SUV.",
